{"results": [{"id": "hp_doc_c00c9db4d7604db01f8673ba348de908b3987c1725efda24d23767c8142f2b82", "title": "Frank C. Huston", "text": "Frank C. Huston (September 12, 1871-October 14, 1959) was an Army Chaplin, songwriter, and music publisher.", "score": 27.048}, {"id": "hp_doc_4af9916d3883a081d0c0e4b0d84fdc91437ee283ca8c10984a1a4488454d030b", "title": "My Own America", "text": "My Own America is a World War II song for voice and piano written and composed by Frank C. Huston. The song was self-published in 1940 by F.C. Huston in Indianapolis, IN.", "score": 23.4543}, {"id": "hp_doc_f8a228edc1e8028e13b34679239d88f5336437e0773b930e8b0dc10701473054", "title": "Tony Huston", "text": "Walter \"Tony\" Antony Huston (born April 16, 1950) is an American actor, writer, and assistant director. He is known for his work on \"The List of Adrian Messenger\" (1963), \"The Dead\" (1987), \"Wise Blood\" (1979), \"\" (2010), \"\" (2008), \"Look Up and Wave Your Glove\" (2005), \"Great Performances\" (2002), \"\" (2001), and \"John Huston and the Dubliners\" (1987). He is the son of John Huston and Enrica Soma, and sibling of Anjelica Huston, Danny Huston, and Allegra Huston. His son is actor Jack Huston.", "score": 14.4842}], "remaining_searches": 2}
